    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0251" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1789</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-14T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1918,
                                noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 14,
                            10.58 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Chinese Government is greatly concerned because of reports from Harbin that
                    General Horvat has issued a government proclamation and that he has concluded a
                    loan with a Japanese bank secured on the Harbin [omission] Chinese Eastern
                    Railway, the proceeds to be used in recruiting troops.</p>
                <p>Semenov intends to take Chita first and supervise but not suspend railway
                    traffic. There is a large secret organization of officers and troops at
                    Changchun who are ready to join him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
